WEBVTT

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.900
When they turn red it means they're roasted.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.400
<b>Trap</b>

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:08.920
It takes a little work to get the little
hermit crabs out of their shells, but...

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.030
The whole inside is edible.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.210
<i>It's a bug.</i>

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:14.810
<i>It just looks like a bug to me.</i>

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.290
The innards are so rich and delicious.

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:21.710
Seriously?

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.480
I-I think I'll try one, too.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.200
We're not in a position to be picky after all...

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.330
That's true.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.090
Y-You're kidding, right?

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.130
I've heard that hermit crabs
are related to king crabs, so...

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.010
they might be really good!

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.100
King crabs?

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.770
If you'd caught those, I'd gladly eat them!

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.100
Well, yeah.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.900
<i>It's like crab... or shrimp...</i>

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.480
The stomach part is like shrimp innards!

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.780
This is surprisingly...

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.240
It's delicious, right?!

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.700
But they're so small it doesn't
feel like we're eating anything.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.310
It would be nice if we could
make soup from them,

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:04.980
but we don't have a pot.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:08.700
It doesn't seem like our cooking
repertoire will increase any time soon.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.020
There's no need to worry about that.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:10.670
Huh?

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.090
After all...

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:18.130
Next, we're going to catch 
and eat some animals.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.070
<i>Huh?</i>

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:30.690
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.490
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.580
We're catching animals?

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.200
Yeah.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.670
When I was walking on the beach

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.960
I found footprints in
the shape of a butterfly.

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.090
Do you know what that means?

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.240
No...

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:37.720
Squirrels.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.860
Squirrels might not weigh very much

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:43.600
but when they run over sand
or snow you can find their footprints.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:46.520
They move like they're jumping
over a vaulting block, so

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.810
their feet leave butterfly-like footprints.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:53.930
Squirrels aren't very gamy
and their meat is tender.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.610
<i>So we are going to eat them.</i>

00:02:55.910 --> 00:03:00.350
Traps are usually the most
efficient way to catch animals.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:03.570
You can do other things
with your time, and it's safe.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:05.230
Safe?

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:10.820
I thought we were gonna have to take
spears and do battle with some wild animal.

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:12.740
This isn't much different...

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.130
It's too cruel.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.750
So... what kind of trap will we use?

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.420
About that...

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.590
<b>Jouichi's</b>

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.590
<b>Survival Training</b>

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:22.590
<b>Traps</b>

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.590
In broad terms, there are
four types of primitive traps.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.100
The first is a snare.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.810
You catch them and pull them up
where they die of strangulation.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.280
The second is a spear, a trap with a stick

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.180
You kill the creature by stabbing it.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.330
The third is a deadfall.

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:37.560
You pin them under a weight so they can't
move and they are crushed to death.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.590
The fourth is a pitfall.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.590
Boom

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:40.950
You drop them in a hole.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:43.260
Strangle... Stab...

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.510
Crush... Drop...

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.310
There are a lot more types, but...

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:53.040
the first time I caught
something I used a deadfall.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.650
She's so excited.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.460
Back then, what I caught was a bear,
but setting up the trap was really—

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.460
Let's just listen quietly...

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:05.210
If we want to survive here, we have
to be ready to catch animals, too.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:06.350
Okay!

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:10.540
It doesn't look like Shion-san
plans to help us with hunting...

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:11.940
Her, huh?

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:14.440
She's always wanting to be babied.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.260
Still... hey, Homare!

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:19.670
Are we really gonna find
anything useful in all this trash?

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:23.190
I was thinking of going
with a snare this time.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.240
We need a thin wire for that...

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.150
Wire, huh...

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.960
Oh, it's just a frog...

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.380
Nice work.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.980
And you didn't even need to hunt it down.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:39.590
Huh?

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.460
Toads have poison under the skin, but...

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:44.540
as long as you skin them, they are edible.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:45.970
<b>Don't eat them</b>

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:48.010
Edible...

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.970
Okay. So, I should catch it, right?

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.390
<i>The warts... are creeping me out...</i>

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.060
Asuka!

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.360
Don't shout all of a sudden!

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.360
Toads have poison glands
behind their ears. Be careful.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.690
Hey! Don't come any closer...

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.240
Don't come this way!

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.660
Stop it!

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.460
Well done!

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.120
No problem.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.060
Come on, Mutsu. Try holding it.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.870
What? It's poisonous, isn't it?

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:23.130
As long as you don't get it in
your eyes, you'll be fine.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.760
With frogs and toads,
 you only eat the legs, so...

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.510
you can process it and
take just the legs back.

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:31.790
Oh.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:33.190
I see...

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.330
<i>Process?</i>

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:39.120
<i>Right. In order to eat this guy,
we have to kill him.</i>

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:42.080
<i>Kill... but how?</i>

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.910
<i>Will I... have to do it?</i>

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.730
Since we're here, let's collect
some water and head back.

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:53.450
All right!

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.010
What's wrong?

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:01.240
It's a burrow.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.250
Animal feces.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.990
They're from an herbivore.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:10.840
What are you doing?

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.510
It's rabbit droppings.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:14.000
It smells like black tea.

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:18.270
Black tea? Well... it doesn't stink...

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:20.080
Let's head back for now.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:22.980
We'll switch our targeted
prey from squirrel to rabbit.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.080
R-Right.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.900
W-We're going to catch rabbits?

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:28.800
What's wrong, Mutsu?

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:33.360
I'm fine!

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:38.820
Welcome back! How did it go?

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.830
It was amazing, Shion-san!

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.460
Asuka-san caught a huge toad!

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.000
Don't bring it this way!

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:46.820
Right, Asuka-san?

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:52.940
Huh? That's weird...

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:55.430
Looks like the toad got away...

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:58.110
I didn't even notice!

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.590
Sorry! I'll be more careful next time.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:04.180
What? How could you not notice?

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:06.370
You're so dense, Asuka!

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:08.320
<i>Homare-san, you're so dense!</i>

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:11.320
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:09.980
Is that so?

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.500
It really is all trash.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:18.290
Can we really catch a rabbit with this?

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:21.210
With the vines and wood we picked up,
we should be able to figure something out.

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:25.070
It's probably a European
rabbit living in that burrow.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:27.710
We'll aim for when it goes in
and out of the burrow to catch it.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.720
We'll use the same trap
we would have for the squirrel...

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:32.790
A snare.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:35.220
You okay?

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.220
Yeah.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:40.230
First, you tie the rope
to a high, supple branch...

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:46.630
This provides the dynamic force.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.250
At the end of the rope you put a toggle...

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:52.440
a stick that serves as a switch.

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.430
Will you hold this for me?

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:55.240
Got it.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:56.820
Asuka.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.850
This is getting kind of exciting, isn't it?

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:02.960
Uh... I'm not quite getting that, but...

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:07.010
Sink a piece of driftwood into
the spot you want to lay your trap.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:10.660
Keep the rope from earlier taut,
and hook it around the stick.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:12.510
Add the stopper...

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:15.390
and make a circle with the loose
rope trailing from the taut rope.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.090
It's finished.

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:18.100
Wow!

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.870
Hey! Can I pretend to be a
rabbit and get caught?

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:23.980
It's dangerous, so don't use your hand.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.100
Got it.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.860
I've been caught!

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.290
A rabbit!

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:33.240
Bunny!

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.240
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.240
Bun...ny... Really?

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:41.300
Rabbit, huh? I wonder what it'll taste like.

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.460
I hope we catch it quick.

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:46.580
But, Asuka-san, you let the toad go, didn't you?

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:49.210
Huh? You knew?

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:53.090
But, meat! My body craves flesh!

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:53.880
Right.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:56.690
This time I will be heartless!

00:08:56.690 --> 00:08:58.300
Really?

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.510
From here, we'll keep
conversation to a minimum.

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:05.640
Rabbits have good ears after all.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:12.940
European rabbit warrens have several
openings spread over several dozen meters.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.860
Let's split into two teams
and set up more traps.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:17.750
It's more efficient that way.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.530
A-All right.

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:25.430
The openings will be in
sunlit areas with grass.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:26.810
Go carefully.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:27.500
I will.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:31.340
If you can't get food for yourself,
you won't survive in the wild.

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:33.020
You understand?

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.270
Y-Yes...

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:36.930
<i>She's scary.</i>

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.930
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.750
You're sure?

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:39.560
Yes, ma'am!

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:44.110
Huh?

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:45.750
Is that...

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.320
It's a burrow!

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:49.540
Asuka-san!

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:52.370
That branch is too thick. It won't bend enough.

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:54.900
Really? But, what else can we do?

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:56.740
What about that one?

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:59.300
It's too high, isn't it?

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.580
We found a burrow, but...

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.000
there isn't a branch that will work...

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.250
Up we go!

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:12.740
Mutsu, are you sure we should be
doing stuff like this unsupervised?

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:16.380
Now... this should work...

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.700
Won't Homare be angry?

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:22.220
Let it down slowly.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:23.470
Here we go...

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:26.890
It...

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.240
It worked!

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:29.100
Really?

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.950
I said not to raise your voices, didn't I?

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:33.570
She's here! The demon instructor!

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:37.150
Not bad.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:38.880
Who thought up the workaround?

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:42.740
There wasn't a good branch at hand, so I...

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.990
I held the log!

00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:48.550
The only thing I worry about
is the speed of the uptake.

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:50.020
So am I.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.640
There's friction between the rope
and the crook of the branch,

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.500
so I'm not sure if it will work.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:57.050
Leave the testing to me!

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:59.400
It's time for Asuka-sama to shine, right?

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.470
I said not to raise your voices.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.390
Here I go...

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:08.710
And I've been caught again!

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:09.690
Bunny!

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:12.610
The speed's not bad. This will work.

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:15.290
Yes! I hope we can catch a rabbit!

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:15.920
Yes.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:17.860
Hey! Help me out!

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.590
You get caught very well.

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:20.930
Really?

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:22.240
I'd expect nothing less from you, Asuka.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:23.240
It's nothing.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:29.080
Next time, Case 5:
A Strange Turban Shell

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:29.970
<b>A Strange Turban Shell</b>
